@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Team-shared conversation views
+
+Conversation folders can be personal or belong to one account team. Server-side
+visibility uses current account/team membership; creator membership and account
+administrator status control writes. Conversation filtering remains viewer-scoped.
+Shared unread counts are recomputed for the viewer to avoid cross-user cache reuse.
+
+The migration preserves existing personal rows. Deleting a creator detaches shared
+filters before asynchronous association deletion; deleting the team removes them.
+The UI exposes audience selection, team identity, read-only member access and
+failure recovery for save/update/delete. Existing personal workflows remain.
+
+Verification: the relevant existing request/model/service and frontend suites,
+request tests in `spec/requests/team_shared_filters_spec.rb`, and a populated
+old-schema upgrade test in `spec/models/team_view_upgrade_spec.rb`. Run the public
+benchmark commands for production build and lint. The external verifier also
+checks a populated base upgrade, HTTP authorization/lifecycle and browser flows.
+
+Tradeoff: shared unread counts favor correctness over a new cache design. There
+are no new sharing roles, account-crossing links or audience-conversion workflows.
